# Context

## Why This Way
Task T069 step one: one shared request path for contract and scenario
modes. The alternative — a parallel scenario pipeline — would fork
validation, negotiation, and commit semantics, which is exactly what
section 9.2 forbids. The seam is one optional GatewayOptions.backend;
absent it, every existing byte of contract behavior is unchanged
(252 gateway tests untouched besides additions).

## Gotchas
- The backend receives only validated context: schema-validated
  parameters keyed by NAME and re-routed by declared location, the
  parsed body (Json view for multipart, text string for text media),
  the matched request media type, and Accept preference order. It
  never sees raw bytes. Query scalars are deserialized with type
  hints, so "5" arrives as number 5 even without a schema ref.
- validateResponse already rejects undeclared statuses
  (status_undeclared), so the scenario path inherits that check for
  free; scenarioCandidateOf still resolves the declared response for
  media negotiation.
- serializeState chains per state object, so one state sees backend
  calls strictly in ingress order (pinned by a concurrency test);
  stateless installs run concurrent.
- domain errors are served responses without a commit payload: the
  exchange is recorded, no transition rides along.

